<title>GERMANY: Waigel-Germany will not exceed EMU deficit level.</title>
<headline>Waigel-Germany will not exceed EMU deficit level.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Friday that Germany would not exceed the deficit level laid down by the Maastricht Treaty for the single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;We will not go over three percent (ratio of deficit to gross domestic product),&quot; Waigel said in a speech to the lower house of the German parliament.</p>
<p>Waigel also said it was &quot;right and proper&quot; to use Bundesbank gold reserves to offset old debt.</p>
<p>&quot;This is not a trick but normal practice,&quot; Waigel said.</p>
<p>He did not mention using gold reserves to reduce running deficit levels.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 260 97 160</p>
